bg3le crash handler: log the fault before unwinding; add an unwinder-free stack scan

On top of 0001-0006. claude-run-2 S024 (07:37:02, the Act 1 -> Shadow-Cursed Lands transition, client
UnloadLevel) died with nothing in the bg3le log. The core shows why: the fault (a call through a freed
Noesis object's vtable on a game worker thread, pc 0x2000000000, rcx = MultiBindingExpression vtable)
entered crash_handler, whose first act was backtrace(); libgcc's _Unwind_Backtrace faulted on the
corrupt stack inside the handler, SIGSEGV was blocked, and the kernel killed the game before logf ran.
Now: signal/pc/registers/[rsp] words first, then a scan of 1024 stack words for bg3/libbg3le code
addresses (an unwinder-free backtrace), then backtrace() last.

